<bioghist encodinganalog="545$a">
<head>Biographical Information
</head>
<p>William Wade Harlowe began his career as an auctioneer in 1968, attending the Reisch American School of Auctioneering in Mason City, Iowa.  After finishing the course in March, 1968, he opened H. &amp; W. Auction Service with Cecil W. Wooldridge in Charlottesville, Virginia.  In 1971, they opened the H. &amp; W. Auction Barn in Fluvanna County, Virginia.  After Wooldridge left the firm, H. &amp; W. became Harlowe Auction, LTD, and in 1980 Harlowe opened the Harlowe Auction Gallery in Charlottesville.  Harlow completed the Certified Auctioneers Institute course of study at Indiana University.  He served as president of the Virginia Auctioneers Association in 1991-1992.  In 1997, Harlowe formed a partnership with Vernon M. Powell, Jr. and created Harlowe-Powell Auction LTD.  in 2003, Harlowe was inducted into the Virginia Auctioneers Association Hall of Fame.  He retired from auctioneering in 2005, along with his wife Roberta Harlowe.
</p>
</bioghist>
<scopecontent encodinganalog="520$a">
<head>Scope and Content
</head>
<p>Papers, 1968-2010, of William Wade Harlowe of Fluvanna County, Virginia, detailing his career as an auctioneer selling antiques, art, automobiles, cattle, chinaware, farm equipment, furniture, jewelry, lumber, real estate, silver, watches, and other items at auctions held in Albemarle, Fluvanna, Nelson, and Orange Counties, and Charlottesville, Virginia, among other places.  Collection contains advertisements, catalogs, magazines, newspaper clippings, sales information, and other documents.
</p>
<p>William and Roberta Harlowe created a five notebook series containing advertisements, catalogs, clippings, sales information, and other documents covering his career between 1968 and 2005.  They then made an abridged two notebook series covering the same time frame.  There is overlap between the two sets, but each does contain information the other set does not.
</p>
</scopecontent>
